# Raised by hand, 2026-08-27 (#512): three error modules grew by a total
# of nine lines when three dead commands in operator-facing errors were
# replaced with instructions that work. `fq recovery`, `fq recover` and
# `fq invocation drop --schema-mismatch` were each one line; what they
# should have said needs two, because the honest answer to a schema
# mismatch is not a command at all — the daemon cannot start, so there is
# no edge and no verb, and the operator has to roll back or delete a
# store.
#
# The `#[error(...)]` text has to live with its error type, so there is
# no module to move it to; extracting a two-line string to dodge a line
# count would be worse code than the count it saved. Raised rather than
# budgeted, per the rule above, so the trade is visible in the diff.
